<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97053" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στοχ-ασμός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>guessing</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελέτης ς</span>. the <i>power of
			guessing</i> which comes from practice. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phlb.</u>
				56a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στοχασμῷ λαμβάνων, ς.
			πινομένη</span>, '<i>quantum sufficit</i>', <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.48
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eup.</u>
				2.21
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ς. ἀεὶ καὶ μᾶλλον ἐξακριβοῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					6.129
				</span></i>
			; as a technical term in Rhet., <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.167S.
			</span></i>, al.; esp. <i>use of circumstantial evidence</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hermog.
				<u>Stat.</u>
				2
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>regard for</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.981b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ πρέποντος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				616b
			</span></i>; <i>attention to</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν εἰρημένων ἀστέρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.28
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>fixing</i> of a hunting-net, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				5.36
			</span></i>.</div>
